TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Final Report (Part 2): Space Mission Design","overview":"Develop a preliminary space-mission design that benefits Australia and report the mission concept and its space-segment elements. Use mission-design software of your choice, supported by hand calculations if useful, and justify the proposed design."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction: mission concept and rationale. Include the following required information: What is the spacecraft's primary mission? Why is the mission needed? How many spacecraft are used and why? Who are the users (operator and customers)?","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Addresses all requirements to a high standard. Detailed descriptions and discussions are included. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Addresses some requirements. Descriptions may feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Many or all requirements are not addressed. Poor descriptions or lack of appropriate referencing."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Main body: mission design. Present a summary of the mission design using software and/or hand calculations as appropriate. Include relevant screenshots and software files in the main body of the report and/or appendix. Include the following information: Where will it launch from, and using which launch vehicle? Why did you choose this option? What type of orbit will you use? What are its characteristics and orbital elements? Will you need to perform any orbital maneuvers? Which ground control facilities will you use? How often will your spacecraft be able to communicate with ground control? How long will the mission last, and what are your plans for EOL?","weight":60,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Demonstrates high level understanding of the design procedure. Design clearly addresses mission and course concepts. Major requirements are all addressed and are well supported with quality evidence (e.g. software screenshots, software files, hand calculations, references from literature). Content is comprehensive, accurate, and persuasive."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Demonstrates adequate understanding of the design procedure. Design may be inconsistent with regards to purpose and clarity of thought or feature errors. Major requirements are addressed but may lack some detail or are not well supported with evidence. Content may not be comprehensive and/or persuasive."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Demonstrates minimal understanding of the design procedure. Major requirements are not addressed and/or lack evidence. Content is incomplete or not persuasive."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Conclusion","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Detailed and appropriate conclusions reached from the evidence provided in the report."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Some conclusions are reached but they may be generic or lack specific detail."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful conclusions reached."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical engineering report structure. The report is easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Executive summary (or abstract) provides a concise overview of the report. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Executive Summary/Introduction"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R3","met":"partial","where":"Executive Summary/Introduction/Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Launch"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Orbit"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Orbit/Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R7","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R8","met":"yes","where":"Mission Duration & EOL"},{"id":"R9","met":"yes","where":"Orbit/Ground Control & Communications"},{"id":"R10","met":"partial","where":"Orbit/Ground Control & Communications (no files/appendix)"},{"id":"R11","met":"partial","where":"Report structure/Bibliography"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Launch","issue":"Kourou latitude is given as 45.05°N; Guiana Space Centre is about 5.2°N, so launch-site geometry discussion is wrong."},{"where":"Orbit","issue":"SSO inclination for 600 km is stated as 87.79°; correct value is about 97.8° retrograde. The graph indicates ~97.8°, so text/table are inconsistent and the defined orbit is not sun-synchronous."},{"where":"Orbit","issue":"Initial RAAN 27.33° is said to indicate launch facility; RAAN at epoch depends on launch time/date, not simply site."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Average contact duration stated as almost 20 min; table mean 580.786 s ≈ 9.7 min (max 12.8 min)."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Claim descending path is constantly sunlit is unsupported; SSO normally has eclipses unless a dawn-dusk local-time orbit is specified."},{"where":"Orbit","issue":"No GSD/swath calculation; text says low resolution 'also desirable' where likely undesirable, undermining altitude rationale."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"No link budget/data rate or ground-station capability analysis to show image data can be downlinked."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"Drag-sail EOL chosen without deorbit lifetime/ballistic coefficient calculation or debris-mitigation compliance demonstration."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"Text says only orbital manoeuvre occurs at EOL but then selects passive drag sail and says no thrusters; does not clearly state no operational manoeuvres."},{"where":"Launch/Bibliography","issue":"Uses Wikipedia '2021 in spaceflight' and tables with citations [49]-[74] absent from reference list; not acceptable source."},{"where":"Report","issue":"No STK/PIGI software files included with report/appendix; only screenshots."}],"overall":"Mission concept is appropriate and report is structured, but credibility is reduced by a wrong SSO inclination, incorrect Kourou latitude, overstated contact duration, missing data-link/swath analysis, missing STK files, and weak referencing.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":6.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Mission and rationale are clearly presented with references, and the single-satellite choice is justified. Users are only implicit (Australian facilities, University of Tasmania, scientists); operator and customers are not explicitly defined, and references are mostly bare URLs. Adequate high.","evidence":[{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Thus, only one satellite is required."},{"where":"Executive Summary","quote":"is operated and accessed from Australia ground facilities"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":30.0,"max":60.0,"reasoning":"Most required design elements are covered and STK evidence is included, but the orbit definition is self-contradictory/wrong: 600 km SSO inclination should be ~97.8°, not 87.79°. Kourou latitude is wrong, mean contact claim is wrong, no link/swath calculations, no STK files. Adequate.","evidence":[{"where":"Launch","quote":"The proposed satellite will thus use the Vega E rocket as a launch vehicle – launched from the Guiana Space Centre Spaceport."},{"where":"Orbit","quote":"requires a mean inclination of $ 87.7924^{\\circ} $"},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"An average contact duration of almost twenty minutes was achieved"},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"The proposed ZYZZsat is small and without thrusters in a low-earth orbit."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":5.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Conclusion restates launch, orbit and ground-station choices, but is brief, omits EOL and key quantitative results, and overclaims that a fully described configuration was constructed. Some specific conclusions but generic.","evidence":[{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"A specific launch vehicle – the Vega E – has been selected although it has not been built yet."},{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"A polar sun-synchronous orbit allows for consistent illumination of the oceans while maintaining a constant sun angle."},{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"The Mt Pleasant Radio Observatory is well-located to receive data from this orbit type constantly and for long durations."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Structure and headings are clear and an executive summary is present, but figures/tables lack numbering/titles, references are bare URLs and do not match in-text citations (e.g. [49]-[74] missing), Wikipedia is used, and grammar slips occur. Adequate low.","evidence":[{"where":"Executive Summary","quote":"This report outlines the intended designs and procedures involved in the construction of a Earth observation satellite"},{"where":"Bibliography","quote":"[6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."},{"where":"Orbit","quote":"STK 3D view of orbit: 12 hours apart"}]}]}
